<%#
  One project on the list. `thumb` is a Maker::Preview or nil (cover). The `.file-cell` +
  data-node-id wiring lets the shared `thumbs` controller poll a pending cover to ready — but only
  when a cover node exists. No cover -> a neutral placeholder, never a forever-spinner: the rail's
  projects icon (structural redesign slice 6; no emoji in the interface).
%>
<div class="project-tile">
  <%= link_to project_path(project), class: "project-card" do %>
    <% if project.cover_node_id %>
      <span class="thumb file-cell" data-thumbs-target="cell"
            data-node-id="<%= project.cover_node_id %>" data-ext="">
        <%= render "files/thumb", thumb:, ext_label: "", url: preview_src(thumb) %>
      </span>
    <% else %>
      <span class="thumb project-thumb-empty" aria-hidden="true"><%= rail_icon(:projects) %></span>
    <% end %>
    <span class="project-name"><%= project.name %></span>
  <% end %>
  <%#
    NEW (stage 4, S4-6; story 1.1). An auto-created project the owner has not opened yet — the only
    feedback discovery has ever had, and the one that works on every backend and for the unattended
    15-minute sweep, which is how discovery actually runs. Both columns come off the row this card
    already holds, so the badge costs no query on the index or on Home.

    `discovered_at.present?` IS the definition of auto-created: Maker::ProjectDiscovery is the only
    writer, and Projects::AdoptionsController leaves it nil on purpose (a project you made is never
    new to you). It clears itself on the first open — ProjectsController#show stamps `opened_at` —
    so nothing has to be dismissed and no state accumulates.
  %>
  <% if project.discovered_at.present? && project.opened_at.nil? %>
    <span class="badge project-new">New</span>
  <% end %>
  <%# THE KIND, WHERE THE PROJECT IS LISTED (stage 4, S4-7). A NON-DEFAULT kind only: `other` is
      the column default, and badging a default is noise -- the same rule the New badge above and
      S4-6's public status badge follow. Beside the New badge rather than inside the link_to, so
      the tile's badges are one group and none of them is part of the card's own click target.
      `.badge` is a component (design-system rule 3); `project-kind` is a qualifier, and
      components.css is not touched. The label comes from Maker::ProjectKind, never `kind.humanize`
      -- "Cnc" is not a word. %>
  <% unless project.kind == Maker::ProjectKind::DEFAULT %>
    <span class="badge project-kind"><%= Maker::ProjectKind.label(project.kind) %></span>
  <% end %>
  <%# THE STATUS, WHERE THE PROJECT IS LISTED (structural redesign §6, slice 6): active, paused and
      done, in the words and component classes the project page's own head uses. `planning` is the
      column default and is never badged, and `archived` is a different list, not a badge. With the
      other badges, OUTSIDE the link — `.project-card .badge` stays empty (projects_flow_test.rb). %>
  <% if project.status.in?(%w[active paused done]) %>
    <span class="badge status-<%= project.status %>"><%= project.status.humanize %></span>
  <% end %>
  <% if project.status == "archived" %>
    <%= button_to "Unarchive", unarchive_project_path(project), method: :patch, class: "linkbtn" %>
  <% end %>
</div>
